  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for reliable delivery at lower cost with fewer defects. They judge you by service levels, savings and people management.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is counting stock and delays for two weeks.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA operations and supply chain: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft reports, summaries and outreach. Routine output becomes common quickly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, relationships and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for drafts; later, own the decisions and the people.
  </p>

